note patterns
; @pos 83 -38
Mutable Instruments Grids patterns

Each bank has 25 patterns with
32 steps each. The Bank slider
takes effect on the next clock
step and keeps the playhead in place.

Each pattern block has one row
per step, with kick (BD), snare (SD)
and hi-hat (HH) levels. The number
in its name matches the source node.

The bank pointer selects a table
of 25 pattern addresses in X/Y order.
Each bank has its own data entry.
X and Y blend nearby patterns in
the selected bank. X increases
right and Y increases downward.

X, Y and density range from 0 to 255.
Density zero mutes that channel.
Higher values include weaker hits.

Gate calculations run on rising clock edges.
The BD, SD and HH outputs pulse
once per triggered step.
The accent outputs pulse on
hits with a level above 192.
Step numbers run from 0 to 31.
noteEnd
note sources
; @pos 149 -23
Imported bank sources

Club, Groove and Jazz/Latin by David Baghurst (Sorrow).
The one-bar Grids tables use the Groove MIDI Dataset by Google LLC (CC BY 4.0).
https://magenta.tensorflow.org/datasets/groove
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/
https://github.com/Eight4aWish/eurorack_daisy_patch_init/tree/22aa3f66ddf98df03e16be5a750c50a5c5e7580b/daisy_grids/tools/grids_firmware

Electronic and Breakbeat by Dylan Bolink (Truchets).
https://github.com/Dylan-Bolink/eurorack/tree/fb3622424b671ea8b3b3159bd6a5a8de89963381/grids

Bank tables are GPL-3.0-or-later.
Converted to 8f4e pattern blocks on 2026-11-10.
Each bank lookup table uses the source map, indexed by X * 5 + Y.
noteEnd
entry main
module sequencer
; @pos -163 0

int* trigger
int step
int nextStep
int previousTrigger
int tick

; Trigger outputs last one sample.
push &outputs:bd
push 0
push end(outputs:)-&outputs:bd
fill

push &tick
push *trigger
call risingEdge
- &previousTrigger
store

push tick
if
push &step
push nextStep
store

push &nextStep
push step
push 1
add
push 31
and
store

call gate
ifEnd
moduleEnd
entryEnd
entry gate
module mapReader
; @pos -96 0
; @home left
int& step &sequencer:step
int bank 0
int** bankPointer &original:cells
int**[] bankTables 6
- &original:cells &club:cells
- &groove:cells &jazzLatin:cells
- &electronic:cells
- &breakbeat:cells
int x 128
int y 128
; Corners: A B
;          C D
int* rowA &pattern04:0
int* rowB &pattern21:0
int* rowC &pattern05:0
int* rowD &pattern01:0
int levelBD
int levelSD
int levelHH

local int balanceX
local int balanceY

push &bankPointer
push &bankTables
push bank
mul 4
add
load
store

push bankPointer
push x
push y
push *step
call selectRows
- &rowA
- &rowB
- &rowC
- &rowD

push x
call mapBalance
localSet balanceX
push y
call mapBalance
localSet balanceY

push &levelBD
push rowA
push rowB
push rowC
push rowD
push 24
push balanceX
push balanceY
call readMap
store

push &levelSD
push rowA
push rowB
push rowC
push rowD
push 16
push balanceX
push balanceY
call readMap
store

push &levelHH
push rowA
push rowB
push rowC
push rowD
push 8
push balanceX
push balanceY
call readMap
store
moduleEnd
module outputs
; @pos -53 0

int& levelBD
- &mapReader:levelBD
int& levelSD
- &mapReader:levelSD
int& levelHH
- &mapReader:levelHH
int densityBD 128
int densitySD 128
int densityHH 128
int bd
int sd
int hh
int accentBD
int accentSD
int accentHH

push &bd
push *levelBD
push densityBD
call densityHit
store

push &sd
push *levelSD
push densitySD
call densityHit
store

push &hh
push *levelHH
push densityHH
call densityHit
store

push &accentBD
push bd
push *levelBD
call accentHit
store

push &accentSD
push sd
push *levelSD
call accentHit
store

push &accentHH
push hh
push *levelHH
call accentHit
store
moduleEnd
entryEnd
